{
  "_comment": [
    "The instrument taxonomy (GDD 5.2) and the fair-value rule for each class",
    "(GDD 5.4). This is data, never Rust constants: it is where a designer",
    "decides what a province is worth relative to a bloodline.",
    "",
    "fair_value = base + sum(terms) + sum(scarcity) , floored, then multiplied by",
    "every modifier whose condition the entity currently meets.",
    "  terms    - weight * fundamental. The ordinary case.",
    "  scarcity - weight / max(fundamental, 1). For claims that grow dearer as",
    "             the thing behind them grows rarer, which is how a commodity",
    "             prices a supply shock.",
    "  modifiers- a multiplier applied while a flag or status reads a given way.",
    "             'when' names the world's own variant, or true/false for a flag.",
    "",
    "'field' keys come from world::fundamentals::Field::key(); an unknown one is",
    "a load error, not a silently ignored line. Every class in the taxonomy must",
    "appear here exactly once (GDD 14, the no-orphan-instrument rule)."
  ],
